  "content": {
    "id": "p37-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "Find any stationary points on $f(x)=2x^3+15x^2+36x-50$ and determine their nature.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Local minimum at $(-2,-78)$; local maximum at $(-3,-77)$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f'(x)&=6x^2+30x+36\\\\f'(x)&=6(x^2+5x+6)\\\\f'(x)&=6(x+2)(x+3)\\end{align*}$$\nAt stationary points,\n$$\\begin{align*}6(x+2)(x+3)&=0\\\\x&=-2\\text{ or }-3.\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}f(-2)&=2(-2)^3+15(-2)^2+36(-2)-50\\\\f(-2)&=-78\\\\f(-3)&=2(-3)^3+15(-3)^2+36(-3)-50\\\\f(-3)&=-77\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}f''(x)&=12x+30\\\\f''(-2)&=12(-2)+30=6>0\\\\f''(-3)&=12(-3)+30=-6<0\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $(-2,-78)$ is a local minimum and $(-3,-77)$ is a local maximum.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 58
  },
